    {
      "id": "practice.together",
      "motifs": ["material_threat", "discovered_attack", "discovered_check"],
      "title": "Look before you move",
      "requires": ["mates.back-rank", "tactics.skewer", "openings.reasons"],
      "steps": [
        {
          "kind": "explain",
          "text": "Use a short scan: is your king safe, what does the opponent threaten, and do you have a check or capture? Test the reply before choosing a move. A discovered attack moves one piece out of the way so a rook, bishop or queen behind it attacks a target. If that target is the king, it is a discovered check. Check what both pieces attack after the move. These positions change the squares from earlier lessons.",
